For divisibility to be a partial order on $\mathbb{N}$ it must be reflexive, antisymmetric, and transitive. \\
reflexivity: $x = 1 \cdot x$ so $x | x$.\\
Antisymmetry: if $x|y \text{ then } y = k\cdot x$, if $y|x \text{ then } x = m\cdot y$, so $y = k\cdot m \cdot y$ so $k \cdot m = 1$ and by previous results this implies $ k = m = 1$. Therefore $x = y$.\\
